    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW266b2wAzfAJMBjD5JpGuLWE)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent; fixes the toggle from #529, #530 and #531 (all merged). Only `devonthink.lua` changes.\n\n## What was wrong\n\n- #531 looked for a tool called \"Text\" inside Tools > Annotate. Sia found in the Hammerspoon console that the real item is **Text Selection**, in the **Mode** menu, so it was never found.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Caps+x finds the item with the exact title `Text Selection`, searched in the whole menu bar (so the menu it sits in does not matter), and chooses it to leave highlight mode.\n- Highlighting counts as on when Highlight Text has a check mark and Text Selection has none. If neither shows a check mark, the last state the key set is used.\n- If Text Selection is not found, an alert says so and nothing changes. The alert after switching is now \"Text Selection\".\n- The colour cache from #517 only holds the Format menu colour paths, never tool names, so it needed no change.\n- The menu bar is read once per press (before, it was read once for the Annotate menu); there is no extra cost.\n\n## Not verified (no Mac or DEVONthink here)\n\n- I could not run the toggle in either direction. It is based on the menu name Sia found. Please check both directions with the manual list below.\n- Whether DEVONthink puts a check mark on Text Selection or Highlight Text. If it does not, only the last-key-press fallback applies, and switching tools with the mouse can fool it. If so, send me `DEVONthink.dumpMenu(\"Mode\")` and the Annotate part of `DEVONthink.dumpMenu(\"Tools\")`.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] Reload Hammerspoon: no error in the console.\n- [x] Open a PDF in text selection mode, press Caps+x: the alert says \"Highlight\" and you can highlight.\n- [x] Press Caps+x again: the alert says \"Text Selection\", the Mode menu shows Text Selection chosen, and you can select text.\n- [x] Repeat a few times: it keeps switching in both directions.\n- [x] Switch to Text Selection with the mouse (Mode menu), press Caps+x: it starts highlighting.\n- [x] Caps+c, the colour keys, Cmd+Z and Cmd+Shift+Z still work.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCTb5QFPFZUd9wzRgq)_",
